{
  "_doc": [
    "Conflation test vectors, shared by the Rust backend and the Flutter app so the two scorers cannot drift apart.",
    "Rust runs them in backend/crates/lunaway-domain/tests/conflation_vectors.rs; the app runs them against its Dart scorer.",
    "The algorithm is specified in docs/conflation.md; every constant it uses is in `parameters` below, and the Rust test asserts that its constants are these.",
    "`names`: input name -> normalised name (fold, abbreviations, generic words removed). `phones` and `websites`: input -> normalised value, null when it identifies nothing.",
    "`cases`: score record `a` against record `b`. `expected` is the decision (merge, review, distinct); `score` is the final score, to be matched within 0.001. Scoring is symmetric: b against a gives the same result.",
    "A record: `source` (source id: osm, atout-france, community), `kind` (taxonomy code), `name` (null when the source gives none), `lat`, `lon` (WGS 84 degrees), and optionally `accuracyM` (metres of position uncertainty, default 0), `osm` (OSM element the record is or cites, e.g. node/123), `wikidata`, `phone`, `website`, `postcode`, `cityCode` (INSEE code).",
    "`why` says what the case pins down; `id` is stable, so a failing case can be named in a commit.",
    "Format version 1. Adding a case or a parameter is compatible; changing a value is a change of the algorithm and goes with both implementations."
  ],
  "version": 1,
